{%- comment -%}
Written out rather than generated by jekyll-sitemap, for three reasons the
plugin gives no control over:

  * it emits page.url, which is /privacy.html - while every link in the estate,
    and every citation inside a contract, uses the extensionless /privacy. Both
    resolve, so listing the .html form would nominate the wrong one as canonical.
  * it walks static files, so assets and PDFs were listed as pages.

Documents with redirect_to are stubs and are skipped automatically, because
jekyll-redirect-from sets no output we want listed.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for page in site.html_pages -%}
{%- assign clean = page.url | remove: "index.html" | remove: ".html" -%}
{%- unless page.redirect_to or page.sitemap == false %}
  <url><loc>{{ clean | absolute_url }}</loc></url>
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
